#> must: # command:  sed  -f
#> not: Alabama
#> not: Iowa
#> source: $!N;$!D
# 16. The last two lines, like tail -2. Pement: sed '$!N;$!D'
# N appends the next line; D deletes up to the first newline and restarts the
# cycle without reading a new line. So the pattern space always holds two
# lines, sliding down the file; on the last line neither runs and both are
# printed. sed '$!d' keeps only the last line; sed '$d' deletes it.
# Try: $!N;$!N;$!D;$!D  for the last three.
$!N;$!D

